==Battleground==
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 4~12 seconds<sup>120f~360f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 2~14 seconds<sup>60f~420f</sup>.
*5 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sunny Celeboodle]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.
**1 [[Bearkini]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Especially on higher crown difficulties, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] is a lifesaver, being able to blitz much of the HP on the bearkini with some meatshielding, often finishing it off. Just one hit from a lv.30 Bahamut Cat is enough to even kill 3 crown Celeboodles in one shot.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] stages, Sandbags on the Cape's Japanese name, Nagisa no Sandbag, is a reference to a song, in this case "[https://youtu.be/qpSOuJ9t_Yo Nagisa no Sindbad]" by [[wikipedia:Pink Lady (duo)|Pink Lady]].

